        "ballot_id": "B002",
        "laureates": [
          "Jacques F. A. P. Miller",
          "Max D. Cooper"
        ],
        "citation": "for discovering distinct T- and B-lymphocyte lineages and their roles in adaptive immunity"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B001",
    "B018"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "B002 remains my preferred configuration. The distinction between T- and B-cell lineages supplied a foundational organizing principle for adaptive immunity, with consequences that now permeate immunology and medicine. The finding is exceptionally mature, repeatedly confirmed, and the proposed two-person attribution is both compact and complementary: Miller's thymus work and Cooper's B-cell lineage biology. It combines conceptual depth, durable explanatory power, and unusually manageable attribution.",
    "case_against": "The historical development involved several experimental systems and other important contributors, so the exact boundary between the two central contributions and related contemporaneous work warrants careful historical assessment.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "perlmann-thomas",
        "point": "Perlmann places B001 first because optogenetics created a durable, broadly influential capability for causal analysis of defined cells and circuits, while acknowledging difficult three-person attribution.",
        "response": "I agree that optogenetics is an extraordinary and mature experimental advance, and it is my leading alternative. However, the unresolved allocation among several foundational contributors is consequential under the three-laureate constraint. B002 offers similarly fundamental biological importance with a more coherent two-person attribution."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "wahren-herlenius-marie",
        "point": "Wahren-Herlenius emphasizes that B037 joins mature GLP-1 biology to transformative, broad clinical benefit, while noting distributed credit from physiology through therapeutic development.",
        "response": "The clinical impact of GLP-1 therapies is compelling, but I share the concern that the supplied record leaves a difficult attribution boundary across peptide characterization, physiology, and drug development. That makes B002's clearer lineage-based conceptual discovery and focused attribution preferable at this stage."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the historical record sufficiently separates the respective contributions of Miller and Cooper from related contemporaneous work."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
}
